# Copy to .env.local. Read by the local Node scripts, never by the browser.

# --- OpenAI (images) ---------------------------------------------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_BASE_URL=
OPENAI_IMAGE_NAME=
# Optional: OpenAI-compatible proxy / relay endpoint. The openai SDK reads this
# variable directly, so the bundled imagegen CLI needs no code change. Keep the
# /v1 suffix unless your proxy documents otherwise. Leave empty to use the
# official https://api.openai.com/v1. If your proxy is a transparent HTTP proxy
# instead, set HTTPS_PROXY (and HTTP_PROXY) rather than this value.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://your-proxy.example.com/v1

# --- Narration (OpenAI speech API) --------------------------------------------------
# Narration talks to exactly one interface: POST {base}/audio/speech. Any
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint works — the official API, a relay, or a local server you run
# yourself. For offline Apple Silicon synthesis there is a separate moss-tts project
# (sibling directory by default) that serves that contract; start it with
# `.venv/bin/python server.py` and see its own README and .env.example.
#
# Endpoint precedence: OPENAI_TTS_BASE_URL -> OPENAI_BASE_URL -> https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_BASE_URL is only a fallback: gen_art.py uses it for the Images API, so repointing
# it would silently redirect image generation too. Set OPENAI_TTS_BASE_URL instead.
# A bare host is completed for you: http://127.0.0.1:8123 becomes http://127.0.0.1:8123/v1
#
# Credential precedence: OPENAI_TTS_API_KEY -> OPENAI_API_KEY. A local server accepts any
# token unless it sets MOSS_TTS_API_KEY, so a placeholder like `local` is fine.
# OPENAI_TTS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8123/v1
# OPENAI_TTS_API_KEY=local
OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts
# Against a local MOSS-TTS server this must name a preset in that server's voices.json.
OPENAI_TTS_VOICE=marin
OPENAI_TTS_SPEED=0.9
# Optional: OPENAI_TTS_INSTRUCTIONS=Read the exact English text warmly and clearly for children.
# Optional executable overrides:
# FFMPEG_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/ffmpeg
# FFPROBE_PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin/ffprobe
# CHROME_PATH=/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome
